WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.700
Lucifer 5B is one hell of a season for Lucifans,
packed with laughter, tears, and destinies

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:07.700
fulfilled.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.910
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm answering the big questions

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:16.869
about how and why that happened to Lucifer,
plus what to expect from Dan, Chloe, Maze,

00:00:16.869 --> 00:00:19.289
and the rest of Team Lucifer in Season 6.

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:21.739
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:21.739 --> 00:00:26.259
God's arrival on Earth is a crucial part of
Lucifer finally having to confront his issues

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:29.220
with his father and the rest of his celestial
family.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.400
Despite the family dinner going badly,
Luci and dad are able to repair their relationship,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.289
with God telling his devilish son that he
does love him just before he reveals he's

00:00:37.289 --> 00:00:40.600
retiring and going to live with the Goddess
in her universe.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.270
This sets up the climactic showdown between
Lucifer and Michael, the two final contenders

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.550
to take over the position of Almighty.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:52.410
The two brothers face off at the LA Memorial
Coliseum, a fitting location given everything

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:56.989
associated with the word Colosseum, the most
famous of which in Rome was home to gladiatorial

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:59.520
battles and public executions.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.239
Michael has the majority of the other angels
on his side;

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:06.160
however, because he doesn't have the unanimous
support needed, his attempt to claim the title

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.160
of God fails.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:12.260
So, he tries to kick off a celestial battle
between the two sides, something neatly foreshadowed

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:16.020
earlier in the ninth episode:
"You have to play in the Family War Zone."

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.020
"Do I?!"

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:21.500
Chloe takes down a couple of angels with melted-down
demon blade bullets, and to avoid further

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.890
bloodshed the twin brothers agree to fight
each other.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:28.940
Michael has the advantage of the Flaming Sword,
the divine weapon that Lucifer used to send

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:33.350
his mother into another dimension, and which
has the power to erase from existence even

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.450
immortal beings like Lucifer.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:39.680
And when Michael slices a cut into Luci's
midriff, it's a call-back to what Dan did

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.300
when he brandished Azrael's blade against
Lucifer in the Season 2 episode "Trip to Stabby

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.300
Town".

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.510
"I know you ate my pudding."

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:51.980
As Lucifer and Michael struggle over control
of the sword, Chloe disables it by pulling

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.070
out the key.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:56.110
And as Lucifer goes to pick up the blade,
Azrael appears.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.310
"I'm sorry, Lu."

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:01.720
Azrael was Ella's special ghost friend in
the Season 3 bonus episode "Boo Normal" and,

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.870
as the Angel of Death, she shows up when somebody
is about to die.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:10.289
Just at that moment, Michael brutally stabs
Chloe with Zadkiel's staff, which is –

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:15.090
ironically but also importantly –
the last remaining piece of the Tree of Life.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:20.230
Chloe dies in Lucifer's arms, accepting she
was never to blame for Dan's death; so free

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.800
of guilt, she reunites with her father in
Heaven.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:27.630
And the sandwiches you see them enjoying together
are an easter egg to the second season episode

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:31.030
"My Little Monkey" when Chloe made the same
ones for Trixie.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.030
Egg sandwiches.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.370
"A Decker family tradition."

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:34.370
[Chloe] So good.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:38.080
"Grandpa used to bring me this sandwich every
Thursday after acting class."

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.340
"So good."

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:44.250
Lucifer refuses to accept Chloe's death, and
decides to go to Heaven to bring her back,

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.730
despite Michael saying his twin will die doing
that.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:50.290
'You know, because of the whole "you're banished
from Heaven and would be instantly incinerated

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:51.790
if you returned" thing.'

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:55.790
Nonetheless, Lucifer flies up to Heaven and
survives the journey thanks to the immortality

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.120
contained in Lilith's ring.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.990
When Lilith blew her immortality into the
ring it transformed from white to black, so

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:06.100
notice how the ring now has little white swirls
in it showing how the protection has been

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.230
activated and its power is being used up.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:14.030
With some help from Mr Said-Out Bitch, Lucifer
finds Chloe and tells her she must go back.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:18.470
Proving his selfless love for her, he takes
off the ring which is protecting him and tells

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:22.290
her:
"I choose you, Chloe, because...

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:23.290
because...

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:25.160
I love you."

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.270
This is a bittersweet moment once more for
Deckerstar fans who've been waiting for those

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.311
three little words.

00:03:30.311 --> 00:03:34.560
"I was so ready to have my Deckerstar dreams
crushed again."

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.800
But the couple are separated again with Chloe
returning to Earth while Lucifer seemingly

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:39.920
burns up.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:44.680
As Chloe comes back to life, Michael tries
to kill her again, but the resurrected Chloe

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:49.720
discovers she now has immense strength,
enough to go up against even an angel like

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.790
Michael, thanks to the necklace part of the
Flaming Sword that she's still holding.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.950
And as she picks up Azrael's Blade, she seems
like she's on the verge of actually killing

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:01.020
Michael –
remember from Season 2 that the blade entices

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.740
those who wield it to murder.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:08.530
However, Lucifer suddenly re-appears, pulling
the detective out of the blade's enchantment.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:10.840
So how did Luci survive?

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:15.660
Lucifer himself doesn't seem to know; however,
there are several clues in Season 5 and earlier

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.379
seasons which can give us an answer.

00:04:17.379 --> 00:04:21.919
First of all, we hadn't heard about Lucifer
dying if he tried to return to Heaven until

00:04:21.919 --> 00:04:24.080
Michael said it in Season 5.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.340
We know Michael lies and plays mind-games,
which we've seen him do to both Amenadiel

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:33.330
and God, and for all we know at some point
he managed to convince his twin of this fact,

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:37.169
meaning that if Luci believed it –
especially if it was tied to his own feelings

00:04:37.169 --> 00:04:41.490
of guilt over his rebellion –
then because angels have the power to self-actualise,

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.349
he might have made himself burn up.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:47.999
And perhaps it's that crucial moment of self-sacrifice
together with him accepting that he really

00:04:47.999 --> 00:04:52.620
does love her, that rids him of all his feelings
of shame about whether he deserved to be accepted

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.620
back into Heaven.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:58.279
That could, in turn, stop him from making
real the belief that he deserved to burn as

00:04:58.279 --> 00:05:02.750
punishment for returning to his family home,
so in effect he saved himself.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:07.720
Also, notice the importance of the word "choose"
in what Lucifer says to Chloe as he gives

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:08.720
her the ring.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.280
"No, you don't have to do that!"

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.780
"I know I don't have to.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:13.930
I choose to."

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:14.930
"What?"

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:15.930
"I choose you."

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.740
That echoes what Chloe said just before dying.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.430
"We make our own choices.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.050
I chose to be here."

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:25.610
Now, we know just how crucial the theme of
"choice" has been throughout the entire series,

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:30.469
after all, Lucifer has so often spoken about
his belief that he has very little or no choice

00:05:30.469 --> 00:05:34.740
in life because of God using him and others
as, what Luci's called, pawns in his game.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:39.090
"If you mean his plan to continually and control
me, then agreed.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.090
It's my Dad's fault.

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.940
I mean, I'm sure it was Him manipulating things
like He always does."

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:48.039
So, it's absolutely huge that Lucifer recognises
in this moment that he does have the power

00:05:48.039 --> 00:05:49.440
to make his own decisions.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:53.680
And I think that his choice to give up his
own life so that Chloe could have a second

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.082
chance on Earth helped make him feel worthy
again and in control of his own existence.

00:05:58.082 --> 00:06:02.620
And I imagine that this was what God hoped
for his fallen son all along.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:03.990
"It's not up to me anymore.

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:05.250
You'll figure it out."

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:09.639
This idea of Lucifer making his own choices
in life and not making excuses for everything

00:06:09.639 --> 00:06:13.159
by blaming his father
was an important point that came up in a previous

00:06:13.159 --> 00:06:17.770
discussion between Luci and Linda about why
he didn't want to tell Chloe he was the devil.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:19.960
"Because she doesn't have a choice, does she?

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:20.960
Neither do I!

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.990
It's all part of His master plan to toy with
us."

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:24.990
"That's an excuse.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:26.889
You're doing the same thing as Him now.

00:06:26.889 --> 00:06:30.749
By not telling Chloe the truth, you're taking
her choice away."

00:06:30.749 --> 00:06:35.759
Tied in with this notion of choosing is Luci
being able to finally tell Chloe that he loves

00:06:35.759 --> 00:06:39.009
her, something he almost did in the mid-season
finale.

00:06:39.009 --> 00:06:43.169
Deckerstar hopes were temporarily scuppered
though after the disastrous family dinner

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:47.599
where God's somewhat cryptic answers to Lucifer's
questions about whether he ever loved him

00:06:47.599 --> 00:06:51.169
made Luci believe he wasn't truly able to
love Chloe.

00:06:51.169 --> 00:06:53.460
"I am my father's son.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:55.530
Like him, I am incapable of love."

00:06:55.530 --> 00:07:00.419
Again, because angels self-actualise, if Lucifer
believed he couldn't love then that would

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:04.899
prevent him from taking the final step in
acknowledging his true feelings for the detective.

00:07:04.899 --> 00:07:09.919
Fortunately, by the time God decides to leave
with Goddess, he admits to Luci that he could

00:07:09.919 --> 00:07:14.780
have been a better father, and then adds:
"I can say something I've wanted to for a

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:15.780
long time.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:16.930
I love you, son."

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:21.069
This was an enormous emotional moment for
Luci as these were things he never expected

00:07:21.069 --> 00:07:24.680
to hear from his father –
remember, Luci said as much after he heard

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:27.639
God Johnson say similarly emotional things
in season 2.

00:07:27.639 --> 00:07:30.849
"You said some things that I think I wish
he'd always said to me.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:31.849
I'm bloody furious.

00:07:31.849 --> 00:07:35.189
'Cause I realized that my father would never
say those things to me."

00:07:35.189 --> 00:07:39.960
But now, finally having this moment with his
real father is the reason why Lucifer's later

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.649
eventually able to say those words to Chloe.

00:07:42.649 --> 00:07:46.809
With Lucifer's miraculous return from Heaven,
all the angels including Michael bend the

00:07:46.809 --> 00:07:50.699
knee to him, signalling he has their unanimous
support as God.

00:07:50.699 --> 00:07:54.740
And when Lucifer raises the Flaming Sword
above his head, you can see the Golden Sun

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:59.550
mural right above him together with Olympic
flames to either side, a nice reference to

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.259
Lucifer's name, the Lightbringer.

00:08:01.259 --> 00:08:02.870
"Oh, my me!"

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:07.849
We can also see how the seeds for this epic
moment were planted all the way back in one

00:08:07.849 --> 00:08:10.779
of Lucifer's therapy sessions with Linda in
Season 1:

00:08:10.779 --> 00:08:13.229
"Before you fell, you were known as Samael.

00:08:13.229 --> 00:08:14.229
The Lightbringer.

00:08:14.229 --> 00:08:18.259
That was a name that connotated your father's
love for you."

00:08:18.259 --> 00:08:22.439
We know that God finally told Luci that he
loved him this season, but in that Season

00:08:22.439 --> 00:08:27.469
1 episode Linda also suggested that when God
cast Lucifer out of Heaven and into Hell it

00:08:27.469 --> 00:08:29.460
was actually a gift:
"It was an act of love.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.419
Because you are his favourite son.

00:08:31.419 --> 00:08:35.509
But here's the thing:
When angels fall, they also...

00:08:35.509 --> 00:08:36.509
rise.

00:08:36.509 --> 00:08:39.520
All you have to do is embrace all that you
are."

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:43.080
She may have thought they were talking in
metaphors at that time, but as it turned out

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.839
the doctor was extremely prescient.

00:08:44.839 --> 00:08:50.221
And by the end of Season 5, Lucifer did indeed
rise to Heaven after accepting that he was

00:08:50.221 --> 00:08:54.980
loved by his father and embracing his true
feelings for Chloe, who notably was also a

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:56.889
gift from God.

00:08:56.889 --> 00:09:00.830
And talking of Chloe, I noticed that Lucifer
made several mentions in the finale that it

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:05.510
wasn't Chloe's time to go yet and that she
was still needed back on Earth, which I think

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:07.660
is setting up a Season 6 plot point.

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:09.680
"The world still needs you, Chloe Decker."

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:15.079
Chloe's second chance at life is also a reminder
that second chances are essentially the overarching

00:09:15.079 --> 00:09:20.050
theme of the series, with Lucifer even showing
mercy to Michael who was willing to kill both

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:21.050
him and the detective.

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:25.700
"In my time here on Earth, I've learned everyone
deserves a second chance.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.260
Even you, Michael."

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:30.769
By the end of Season 5,
Maze too found she was given a second chance

00:09:30.769 --> 00:09:34.569
at happiness when Eve returned to her and
our favourite demon discovered she'd grown

00:09:34.569 --> 00:09:38.880
a soul through the time she'd spent building
relationships with people on Earth.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:43.670
As for Linda, she reconciles with her grown-up
daughter who she gave up as a teenage mother;

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:47.579
and through her relationship with Amenadiel,
Linda has taken a second chance to form a

00:09:47.579 --> 00:09:49.660
family with him and Charlie.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:54.209
And when God comes to appreciate how he failed
his wife by neglecting her through his work,

00:09:54.209 --> 00:09:58.259
he takes the opportunity of a second chance
to build a new life with her by going to live

00:09:58.259 --> 00:09:59.259
in her universe.

00:09:59.259 --> 00:10:04.190
Over the course of the series, Dan has also
reformed himself and grown to be a better

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:05.190
person.

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:09.600
He was, of course, cruelly killed in the fifth
season and, when Amenadiel visited Heaven,

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:13.899
he discovered Dan wasn't there as his lingering
feelings of guilt about his past mistakes

00:10:13.899 --> 00:10:15.860
in life had taken him to Hell.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:19.990
However, I think that with some help from
Team Lucifer in Season 6, Dan will find a

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:24.279
way to leave Hell and ascend to Heaven, just
like Mr Said-Out Bitch managed to do.

00:10:24.279 --> 00:10:26.060
"I know I took your advice.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.800
I faced my family.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:28.810
My guilt."

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.009
"You went through the door."

00:10:31.009 --> 00:10:32.089
"Yep, finally.

00:10:32.089 --> 00:10:33.190
And boom, Heaven!"

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:36.829
Mr Said-Out Bitch's arc is a mini version
of Lucifer's.

00:10:36.829 --> 00:10:41.320
They were both stuck in Hell in the first
episode of Season 5, with Luci agreeing to

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:45.519
help Lee find the source of his guilt which
stemmed from the time he felt too ashamed

00:10:45.519 --> 00:10:48.010
to visit his family for his sister's baby
shower.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:52.690
Although Lucifer berates Lee for his failings,
it's clear that the scene is meant to illuminate

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:55.930
Luci's innermost feelings about his own celestial
family.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:11:00.310
"If you go through that door, it's only a
matter of time before you screw up again.

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:02.750
And so you'd rather stay away for all eternity."

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:04.550
"This isn't just about me, is it?

00:11:04.550 --> 00:11:06.170
Whose Hell is this anyway?"

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:10.860
Like Lee, Lucifer decided to go through the
door to his family home when he faced up to

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:14.971
his shame and risked everything by returning
to Heaven, which in turn broke him out of

00:11:14.971 --> 00:11:17.300
his own metaphorical Hell loop.

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:21.279
Likewise, Dan will need to find the key to
walking through the door that's keeping him

00:11:21.279 --> 00:11:22.629
in his own personal Hell.

00:11:22.629 --> 00:11:28.069
It'll be interesting to see what in particular
Dan feels so guilty over in Season 6 and who'll

00:11:28.069 --> 00:11:31.040
be able to visit him to help him escape his
own Hell loop.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:35.180
And like many other Lucifans, I'll be doing
another re-watch of the show to look for more

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:36.810
clues before Season 6.

